From 06ba666b660daf9bab806370e98300a22f4f42bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raiju contributors <raiju@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:19:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: streamed response bodies with Bun's API: new
 Response(stream) for a ReadableStream with an underlying source (start with
 enqueue, close and error, cancel when the client leaves), sent with
 transfer-encoding: chunked as each chunk is enqueued, in every worker

Bun.serve could only answer with a body that was complete when the handler returned. A
handler now returns a Response whose body is a ReadableStream made with an underlying source:
the head goes out with transfer-encoding: chunked, and each enqueued chunk follows at once. A
client that leaves cancels the stream. text() and bytes() on such a response read it whole.

Tests: tests/http.rs streams /stream and /endless from tests/http/app.tov (chunked framing,
chunks spread over time, a client leaving mid-stream cancels the source and the next request
is served, twelve streams on three workers); tests/run/native_stream_response.tov drains a
pushed stream with text() and bytes() and checks that a failing stream rejects.
